## Facts
- Round-3 aggregate: all 14 Java/Kotlin samples completed, then the final scan
  `rg -n "$FORBIDDEN_SAMPLE_PATTERN" "$SAMPLES_DIR" -g '*.java' -g '*.kt'` matched two sites
  (`zlink-work/c016/logs/gate-final-java-3-aggregate.log:1062-1064`). Read the pattern definition at
  the top of `framework/languages/java/samples/run_samples.sh` and the sample guide's rule it encodes
  (`framework/doc/framework/java/guide/**` samples section, read-only) so the replacement follows the
  intended convention (samples must not poll with sleeps; wait on the framework's completion/lifecycle
  primitives).
  1. `framework/languages/java/samples/java/DeliveryDispatch/Server/Dispatch/src/test/java/systems/zlink/samples/deliverydispatch/server/dispatch/DispatchWorkerDeadlineTest.java:59`
     — `TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.sleep(SampleTimings.CourierDecisionTimeout.toMillis() + 100)` added by the
     campaign commit `ed156f5983` (courier offer deadline starts after the status publish). Replace
     the wall-clock sleep with a deterministic wait: e.g. a controllable clock/scheduler injected into
     the worker, or waiting on the expiry queue with a bounded timed poll (`offers.takeExpired()`
     semantics — check how the worker publishes expiry) so the assertion "status publication time
     must not consume the courier decision timeout" is preserved without sleeping.
  2. `framework/languages/java/samples/java/TicTacToe/Client/src/main/java/systems/zlink/samples/tictactoe/client/TicTacToeClientScenario.java:306`
     — a `Thread.sleep(100)` polling loop waiting for "runner lifecycle completion" (since
     `e4442b8456`, 2026-08-30). Replace the polling with the proper wait on whatever signals lifecycle
     completion (a `CompletionStage`/latch from the framework runtime, or a `WatchService` if it polls a
     file the runner writes) with the same overall deadline and the same `IllegalStateException` on
     timeout. Compare with the Kotlin TicTacToe client and the other languages' TicTacToe clients for
     the established pattern (read-only).
- Do not touch other `sleep` sites the scan does not flag.

